From 61817dff6a2dc6f306db8d6bb3a72efbec6d140c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giorgos Sarigiannidis <contact@gsarigiannidis.gr>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:33:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Conflicts list: a side panel beside the merge, with a
 layout switch

The Conflicts list can sit in a side panel next to the file being merged,
as well as in a tab of its own. A switch in the header bar flips between
the two at any time and saves the choice in the conflicts-layout setting,
so the list opens in the layout used last (tabs at first). Only the list
moves: the merge tabs stay notebook pages
in both layouts, with their tab strip hidden in the side view, since a
merge view moved to another container re-runs one-time setup in its
widgets.

In the side view, clicking a file shows its merge, open files carry a dot,
Accept yours and Accept theirs show on every row, clickable on the
selected one, and
saving opens the next unresolved file (Save and next file). From the list,
saving never closes the window. Closing the window asks the list after
every tab and only when all agreed, since its close ends Meld with its exit
status; both decisions are pure functions tested in test_conflicts.
